tests/ui/check/ok_uncertainty_comparison_warning.sky:5:6: warning: comparing an uncertain value compares only its nominal value
  |
5 | if a > b:
  |      ^ `>` ignores the uncertainty
  |    - this value may carry an uncertainty
  = note: a comparison looks at the central values alone, so `a < b` can hold even when `a` and `b` agree within their uncertainties
  = help: to ask whether two values agree, compare their difference with its uncertainty: `abs(nominal(a - b)) < 2 * uncertainty(a - b)`

tests/ui/check/ok_uncertainty_comparison_warning.sky:7:13: warning: comparing an uncertain value compares only its nominal value
  |
7 | print(a - b < 0.1 m/s^2)
  |             ^ `<` ignores the uncertainty
  |       ----- this value may carry an uncertainty
  = note: a comparison looks at the central values alone, so `a < b` can hold even when `a` and `b` agree within their uncertainties
  = help: to ask whether two values agree, compare their difference with its uncertainty: `abs(nominal(a - b)) < 2 * uncertainty(a - b)`
